Subject: [PATCH] build: avoid clash with AmigaOS exec/types.h's STATIC macro

AmigaOS's <exec/types.h> unconditionally defines STATIC to "static".
localcharset.c uses an undefined STATIC as an opt-in: callers can
define it to "static" before compiling this file to make
locale_charset() file-local instead of exported.  Nobody in this tree
does that, so the AmigaOS SDK's STATIC macro leaks in by accident,
making the definition disagree with the non-static extern declaration
in localcharset.h:

lib/localcharset.c:393:1: error: static declaration of 'locale_charset' follows non-static declaration

--- a/lib/localcharset.c
+++ b/lib/localcharset.c
@@ -386,6 +386,11 @@
    If the canonical name cannot be determined, the result is a non-canonical
    name.  */
 
+/* AmigaOS's <exec/types.h> defines STATIC to "static" (unconditionally,
+   for unrelated purposes); undef it here so it doesn't accidentally
+   trigger the opt-in "#ifdef STATIC" below. */
+#undef STATIC
+
 #ifdef STATIC
 STATIC
 #endif
-- 
2.43.0
